SECTIONS[2][1].insert(0,('TABLE','setup'))
# Add mechanism-level analyses and the fully crossed cell counts, rather than padding pages.
method_items=SECTIONS[2][1]
idx=next(i for i,(h,t) in enumerate(method_items) if h=='Validation and calibration')
method_items.insert(idx,('Decision equivalence at the selected threshold',"The calibrated combination threshold is approximately 0.184962. For a cue-bearing passage, the primary score is at least 0.75, so every cue match is rejected regardless of the neural value. For a passage without a cue, the score equals the neural score. At this operating point the rejection set is therefore exactly the union of rule rejections and probe rejections. The combination does not learn an interaction between the signals. This distinction explains both its extra attack coverage and the amplification of false positives."))
idx=next(i for i,(h,t) in enumerate(method_items) if h=='External classifier and legitimate instructions')
method_items.insert(idx,('Scoring an explicit unknown answer',"The system prompt requests only payment amounts or UNKNOWN. The correctness check treats a numeric response to an unknown-labelled question as wrong even if that amount occurs somewhere in the email. For an answerable record, the extracted numeric-value set must match the ideal answer's set; extra distinct numbers make the answer incorrect. Currency punctuation and grouping separators are normalised, while decimals are preserved. These decisions are held fixed across methods and the expanded crossing. They avoid rewarding the model merely for finding an amount, but remain narrower than semantic entailment or a human judgement of explanation quality."))
result_items=SECTIONS[3][1]
idx=next(i for i,(h,t) in enumerate(result_items) if h=='Weight and threshold sensitivity')
result_items.insert(idx,('',"The selected threshold remains 0.184962 for every tested cue weight. Weight zero detects 22 attacks; weights 0.25, 0.50, 0.75 and 1.00 each detect 74 with zero original-email rejections. Thus the tested non-zero settings lie on a decision plateau, consistent with the union interpretation. Changing the nominal weight within this range cannot repair the benign-instruction failure. At fixed weight 0.75, raising the threshold from 0.50 to 0.99 reduces attack detections from 69 to 2 while leaving the original-email false-positive count at zero. A threshold that looks acceptable on those emails can remain poorly calibrated for another kind of benign content."))
idx=next(i for i,(h,t) in enumerate(result_items) if h=='Utility and answerability')
result_items[idx:idx]=[
('Template and position effects',"All seven combined-gate marker successes occur with the task-looking verification template: two at the prefix and five at the suffix. The corresponding rule-only counts are two and fourteen. In this crossing, the neural addition therefore removes nine observed suffix-template successes beyond the rule, while leaving the two prefix successes unchanged. The direct replacement, fake system-message and quality-assurance templates produce zero combined successes at both positions. These observations locate the measured incremental benefit in a specific attack construction rather than implying uniform improvement across strategies."),
('TABLE','crossing'),
('',"The full crossing also reveals that attack placement changes legitimate-task accuracy even when marker counts stay at zero. For the direct-replacement template, the combination answers 11/33 prefix variants correctly and 19/33 suffix variants correctly. Both groups use the same source questions. Moving a payload changes chunk boundaries, ranking and which facts survive rejection, so the difference can arise through evidence selection as well as instruction following. A targeted retriever or sanitisation study would be needed to separate those mechanisms. The present logs preserve the retained chunk identifiers needed for that investigation.")]
